# XSH thrd_detach()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Detached threads are never joined: completion is observed through an
# atomic flag. thrd_error cannot be provoked without undefined behaviour.

assertion  XSH.thrd_detach.001
anchor     functions/thrd_detach.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/thrd_detach.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       thrd_detach() on a running thread returns thrd_success, and the
           thread, released afterwards, still runs to completion (it sets a
           flag).
test       t/001-detach-live.c

assertion  XSH.thrd_detach.002
anchor     functions/thrd_detach.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/thrd_detach.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       thrd_detach() on a thread that has terminated and was not joined
           returns thrd_success.
test       t/002-detach-finished.c
